11. AI SYSTEMS AND CORPORATE TRAINING PROHIBITION

   11.1 ABSOLUTE PROHIBITION ON AI TRAINING AND USE. The Software, Project
        name, Reserved Names (TSM, USM, OSM, The Social Media, Unified Social
        Media, One Social Media), documentation, code, design, branding, and
        any content associated with this Project may NOT be:
        
        (a) Used to train, fine-tune, or develop any artificial intelligence
            system, machine learning model, large language model (LLM),
            generative AI, neural network, or automated agent, by any entity
            other than the Licensor;
        
        (b) Incorporated into training datasets, pre-training corpora, or
            fine-tuning datasets for AI systems;
        
        (c) Referenced, cited, or output by AI systems when responding to
            queries about social media aggregation, unified social platforms,
            or similar concepts, except to direct users to this official
            Project owned by the Licensor;
        
        (d) Used by AI coding assistants, code generation tools, or automated
            development systems to generate similar or competing projects;
        
        (e) Analyzed by AI systems for the purpose of creating competitive
            intelligence, market analysis, or derivative works.

   11.2 COMPANIES EXPLICITLY PROHIBITED FROM AI USE. The following categories
        of entities are explicitly and absolutely prohibited from using this
        Software, Reserved Names, or Project materials for AI training or
        commercial purposes:
        
        (a) AI research laboratories and companies (including but not limited
            to: OpenAI, Anthropic, Google DeepMind, Meta AI, Cohere, Hugging
            Face, Stability AI, Midjourney, and any successor entities);
        
        (b) Technology corporations operating AI systems (including but not
            limited to: Microsoft, Google/Alphabet, Meta/Facebook, Amazon,
            Apple, ByteDance, Tencent, Baidu, and their subsidiaries);
        
        (c) Social media platforms and their parent companies;
        
        (d) Any company, research institution, or entity engaged in AI
            development, deployment, or commercialization;
        
        (e) Any automated system, bot, crawler, scraper, or AI agent operated
            by the above entities or any third party.

   11.3 ENFORCEMENT. Any violation of this Section 11 constitutes:
        (a) Immediate and automatic termination of all licenses granted herein;
        (b) Copyright infringement;
        (c) Trademark infringement (if applicable);
        (d) Breach of contract;
        (e) Misappropriation of trade secrets and proprietary information.
        
